{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/52522-regaining-willpower","id":52522,"title":"Regaining Willpower","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-01-18T10:31:07-08:00","id":52522,"title":"Regaining Willpower","content":"You can gain willpower from Dirge/Mask, Touchstones etc<br /> <br /> As a Kindred, am I right in thinking you can't get it through rest? I can't find any reference to being able to do so, only that Strix can't because they don't need rest - which made me wonder if Vampires can.<br /> <br /> I think I might make a slight house rule in regaining willpower to make it slightly easier. My reasons for doing it is that I have some players who might play their Dirge a bit too well (for examplem in order to maximize willpower gain which could be difficult at times. Another reason is I like the idea of having a game of higher BP characters who aren't Ordo Dracul and can actually live off humans rather than lose a WP for each single Vitae they get back.<br /> <br /> On the other hand I do want and like the idea of people paying much more attention to their dirge and mask, virtue and vice (although promises of beats will always help with that)<br /> <br /> I know this isn't Masquerade too, but in that game where you could spend exp/points on upping your Willpower (rather than regaining lost WP) I had a whole bunch of players with very high willpower scores who still didn't spend it for fear of not getting it back quick enough (that was a ST/Player communication problem though to be honest)<br /> <br /> How has it been in play for people? - whilst it's meant to be relatively difficult to regain WP, as so many things require it has it at all been a bit too scarce at times for comfort?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:8px\"><b>Danny James - FL Editor, Writer, &amp; Proofreader - @AlienStoneDog<br /> - Onyx Path, Pinnacle, C7, TAG</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/510-meetsintaverns","name":"MeetsInTaverns","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar510_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"127"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-18T10:39:01-08:00","id":52528,"title":"","content":"Well, since vampires follow human rules whenever those have not been overwritten by vampire template rules (healing for example) I believe that you do regain one willpower when you rest.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-18T10:42:20-08:00","id":52537,"title":"","content":"I thought that might be the case but it's not stated anywhere specific under daysleep. It's very obvious that many things cost wp, but there's no easy sidebar saying x gains you wp, see page y.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:8px\"><b>Danny James - FL Editor, Writer, &amp; Proofreader - @AlienStoneDog<br /> - Onyx Path, Pinnacle, C7, TAG</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/510-meetsintaverns","name":"MeetsInTaverns","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar510_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"127"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-18T11:01:42-08:00","id":52559,"title":"","content":"Double checked. Looked up every instance of &quot;Willpower&quot; in blood and smoke. Since it's meant to be a standalone and it says nowhere that you regain a willpower point during rest, it looks like you're right. However, I also think that there's a chance that it's a mistake and it was forgotten to write it in. On the other side, it might be a conscious choice, which is there to encourage anchor usage. <br /> <br /> Can anyone confirm which is it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-19T03:01:06-08:00","id":53094,"title":"","content":"I'm going to allow the gaining back 1 wp a night, I think it's a fair thing. It still allows high BP to function by feeding on humans but still puts them in a position (which makes sense thematically) where they don't go around blatantly using vitae because it would be harder to regain vitae without burning wp and having to really indulge in their vices.<br /> <br /> But hey, I'm also houseruling that you don't need to feed on supernaturals until bp 7 anyway.<br /> <br /> And that you don't necessarily get conditions from succeeding in a humanity roll - but that's beside the point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:8px\"><b>Danny James - FL Editor, Writer, &amp; Proofreader - @AlienStoneDog<br /> - Onyx Path, Pinnacle, C7, TAG</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/510-meetsintaverns","name":"MeetsInTaverns","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar510_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"127"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-19T05:40:38-08:00","id":53137,"title":"","content":"I think it's reasonable and i like its consequences, MeetsInTaverns, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/49180-list-of-errata/page2\">but I'd like to hear from the developers about this matter.</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/7019410/Images/Ex3%20KS%20Badge.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1866-ophion","name":"Ophion","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-19T12:07:22-08:00","id":53362,"title":"","content":"Vampires don't get Willpower back from resting by default. One of the things Willpower represents is strength of self, parallel to Humanity. You get it for affirming who you are, who you pretend to be, and what you're connected to. Being a vampire is spiritually exhausting, and you have to emphasize those things in order to regain what normal people gain from rest.<br /> <br /> I say that with the following caveats:<ul><li>When significant downtime has passed (say, you skip a week of in-character time, or conclude a significant piece of your story and pick up later), it's reasonable to just refill everyone's Willpower, making the assumption they've been out interacting with their Anchors while off-screen.</li> <li>I don't think it does any harm to allow Kindred to regain Willpower from rest, it's just not the default for the reasons I expressed.</li> </ul>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-19T12:35:26-08:00","id":53384,"title":"","content":"Awesome as always Rose","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:8px\"><b>Danny James - FL Editor, Writer, &amp; Proofreader - @AlienStoneDog<br /> - Onyx Path, Pinnacle, C7, TAG</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/510-meetsintaverns","name":"MeetsInTaverns","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar510_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"127"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-19T15:06:12-08:00","id":53491,"title":"","content":"Makes sense, thank you Rose!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/7019410/Images/Ex3%20KS%20Badge.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1866-ophion","name":"Ophion","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-19T16:41:13-08:00","id":53538,"title":"","content":"Interesting. I had thought it was a mistake. It is not the first time that the devs weren't clear enough with the rules*. I guess this means that elders that don't quite seem to retire to torpor would have to be quite active (or retain many touchstones) to continue feeding on restricted blood. Still, this means that a coil that enables a vampire to recover willpower during daysleep is now up for grabs (I might want to consider it for the mystery of civility that I'm working on).<br /> <br /> *One example I recall was how some people came to the conclusion that the Requiem 1.0 rules allowed ghouls to remain immortal so long as they did not spend their last point of vitae. The rules did not explicitly state that the point of vitae had to be used up in the process, only that a ghoul have a point of vitae stored and was able to spend a point of willpower.<br /> <br /> Edit: Wait. This will require some considerations as to what a sanctified priest needs to do recover willpower. They can't cast rituals without it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":536,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/536-divinewrath","user":"DivineWrath","date":". 01-19-2014, 07:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/536-divinewrath","name":"DivineWrath","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar536_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"326"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-19T20:06:51-08:00","id":53651,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DivineWrath</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/52522-regaining-willpower?p=53538#post53538\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Edit: Wait. This will require some considerations as to what a sanctified priest needs to do recover willpower. They can't cast rituals without it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I assume, you change your Mask or Dirge to 'Monster' or 'Mystic' or something that you that fits the activities that you will be doing in your search, and execution of awesome mystical power. Though, it does make Cruac seem to be a better option.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u><b>My Homebrew</b></u><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1PLu_eTg03h4ogiTSGSkzEB7T_1YpB9_VkhHmgZN41-I/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Star Wars d10</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">T</a><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">he Fallen for Demon: the Descent</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-TDr4NF_5cUn-In2vjI9P5LTKqsu9B4-OMxbnbaTgT8/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Requiem for a Masquerade: VtR 2e Cainite Conversion</a> (<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1HpKi5giBNsQrZRLIRRjaCe7sHVm1Q13ravVYlE45Dbw/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Vampira Roma</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1601-dreaminggod","name":"Dreaminggod","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"745"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-19T20:56:00-08:00","id":53688,"title":"","content":"Well, living your Mask or Dirge or interacting with your Touchstone should not really be that much more difficult than getting 1-5 points of Vitae, in fact it is probably easier. These activities are also less of a danger to your Humanity and the Masquerade!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Politeness is the lubricant of social intercourse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","name":"saibot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1063"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-19T21:10:53-08:00","id":53702,"title":"","content":"Very true! It also highlights the difference for the two Sorceries rather well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u><b>My Homebrew</b></u><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1PLu_eTg03h4ogiTSGSkzEB7T_1YpB9_VkhHmgZN41-I/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Star Wars d10</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">T</a><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">he Fallen for Demon: the Descent</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-TDr4NF_5cUn-In2vjI9P5LTKqsu9B4-OMxbnbaTgT8/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Requiem for a Masquerade: VtR 2e Cainite Conversion</a> (<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1HpKi5giBNsQrZRLIRRjaCe7sHVm1Q13ravVYlE45Dbw/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Vampira Roma</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1601-dreaminggod","name":"Dreaminggod","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"745"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-20T02:53:15-08:00","id":53856,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>saibot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/52522-regaining-willpower?p=53688#post53688\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, living your Mask or Dirge or interacting with your Touchstone should not really be that much more difficult than getting 1-5 points of Vitae, in fact it is probably easier. These activities are also less of a danger to your Humanity and the Masquerade!</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree I think.<br /> <br /> Replacing 1-5 WP between sessions this way would be a damn good way for me to get folk to do some downtown for me (unless you're of the school that would replenish WP between sessions).<br /> <br /> I think I'd like to see some more expansion though, further ideas on how touchstones can replace lost willpower. It says for 1pt that it should err on the side of the player. Of course touchstones are varied and can't come down to a hard a fast rule but what would people think the minimum for a dot of returned wp would require - calling up your TS and asking how they've been this week? Going around for tea, or following them around in a stalking kind of way waiting for a chance to meaningfully interact with them?<br /> <br /> I know you gain WP from defending your touchstone as well. (page 88)<br /> <br /> I think it's all very interesting, I like that WP is so very important, but I am personally going to run with WP returned during rest - else I foresee anything that drains your WP (either through your own exertions or via supernatural power) is a very potent way of defeating kindred.<br /> <br /> I also want to encourage my players to act like their Mask/Dirge and interact with their Touchstones, but I don't want them to be preoccupied with them to the extent of the story by fear of running out of willpower and being ineffective in the game.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:8px\"><b>Danny James - FL Editor, Writer, &amp; Proofreader - @AlienStoneDog<br /> - Onyx Path, Pinnacle, C7, TAG</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/510-meetsintaverns","name":"MeetsInTaverns","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar510_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"127"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-20T08:09:13-08:00","id":53998,"title":"","content":"One compromise I would suggest is making &quot;Willpower from rest&quot; a Merit effect for vampires. That is like having your cake and eating it too!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Politeness is the lubricant of social intercourse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","name":"saibot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1063"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-20T08:38:39-08:00","id":54021,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>saibot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/52522-regaining-willpower?p=53998#post53998\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One compromise I would suggest is making &quot;Willpower from rest&quot; a Merit effect for vampires. That is like having your cake and eating it too!</div> </div> </div> </div>Heh, could do, but I just know that ALL my players will be wanting to take Acute Senses anyway <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Gotta leave some merit points for something","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:8px\"><b>Danny James - FL Editor, Writer, &amp; Proofreader - @AlienStoneDog<br /> - Onyx Path, Pinnacle, C7, TAG</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/510-meetsintaverns","name":"MeetsInTaverns","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar510_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"127"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-21T00:22:26-08:00","id":54515,"title":"","content":"But I think in all honesty that I'm going to be giving back WP a lot, as long as they're paying lipservice to the Dirge/Masquerade/Touchstones<br /> <br /> After all, it's not like I'm not the one putting them in situations where they really need to spend WP<br /> <br /> And you can't blame one of my players for their inability to never roll more than a 7.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:8px\"><b>Danny James - FL Editor, Writer, &amp; Proofreader - @AlienStoneDog<br /> - Onyx Path, Pinnacle, C7, TAG</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/510-meetsintaverns","name":"MeetsInTaverns","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar510_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"127"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-27T02:56:53-07:00","id":900801,"title":"","content":"Hi everyone! What is considered an average amount of Willpower regained from Mask and Dirge (we don't currently use Touchstones) per 3-hour session per player character? (by you / by the book / by the designers)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6216-p-czigany","name":"p.czigany","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-27T06:09:14-07:00","id":900870,"title":"","content":"I allow my players to regain willpower by sleeping. Mostly because they need it when they're awake more often than not.<br /> <br /> As for an average of willpower from dirge/mask, I wouldn't know, but for my session, not that much. It doesn't come very often as my players don't really push the issue often. Their mask and dirge are general roleplay hints (and ways for me to predict what they'll do so it plays out just as planned) more than ways to regain WP.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7104-s-brechen","name":"S. Brechen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-27T12:57:51-07:00","id":901297,"title":"","content":"I don't think I've ever had a player in my games regain it via mask/dirge. So generally they don't use much WP. And I just refresh whenever we do a time skip of a couple days.<br /> <br /> They just feel like it's kind of forced to work them in. I dunno.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-27T14:00:20-07:00","id":901356,"title":"","content":"Thank you S. Brechen and Maina!<br /> <br /> Do you think regaining Willpower from someone's Mask has anything to do with the Masquerade? (&quot;Any time a vampire overcomes a small hurdle in defense of her Mask, she gains a point of Willpower.&quot;) Do you have to actively defend the Masquerade to deserve the point of Willpower?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6216-p-czigany","name":"p.czigany","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-27T14:59:54-07:00","id":901432,"title":"","content":"Not the way I understand it. The Masquerade is the whole collective effort of the vampires to not let mortals know vampires are all around them. The way I see it, The mask isn't just the face a vampire shows humans, it's the part of themselves they consciously or unconsciously show everyone, vampire or human. The Dirge would be what they keep for themselves or what they only allow themselves to be around people they trust. Regaining willpower from your mask is just a matter of how mcuh you're willing to risk to keep people from seeing beyond what you want them to see. Like, if a vampire has mask : mastermind, he'll get his kicks from people seeing him as a clever dude who's really difficult to outsmart. If one of his plans start to completely fall appart, he might regain all his willpower if he risks his unlife doing damage control and tying up loose ends so that nobody ever knows he messed up.<br /> <br /> People might disagree on the exact meaning, but I'm pretty sure it's not about the masquerade. One of my player's character has the Mask : Harmless and the Dirge : Vindictive. She's a former vampire hunter turned vampire herself. She tries to appear pretty harmless to everyone she meets but has a pretty mean streak when she feels people have crossed her, including (in my game, mostly) vampires. She's mostly gained willpower by being vindictive so far, but if she, for example, let herself get beat up by someone without really trying to fight back, she'd regain willpower because she wouldn't look like a threat.<br /> <br /> This is an example, but the mask and dirge don't have to be opposite or really different. Again, though, I wouldn't be too attached to that. These are two ways to see your character, but any believable character won't be described by just two words.<br /> <br /> This is beside the point, but I think it's also pretty normal for character to change their mask or dirge occasionnally if it's justified. One of my players who had the dirge &quot;humanist&quot; (she would always try to favor humans, seeing vampires as monsters that needed to be killed if they didn't try really hard to not feed on humans) asked to change it after she found out about the Strix, how they were potentially way worse than the vampires and that vampires were maybe one of the few things that had a shot at fighting them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7104-s-brechen","name":"S. Brechen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-27T16:41:36-07:00","id":901516,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>S. Brechen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/52522-regaining-willpower?p=901432#post901432\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not the way I understand it. The Masquerade is the whole collective effort of the vampires to not let mortals know vampires are all around them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eeeyyyyhhhh, that's kind of an outdated concept of the Masquerade at this point. That's certainly what it means in VtM, and 1e kind of held onto it, but 2e has really doubled down on the idea that the supernatural doesn't need a massive concerted effort to keep itself secret. Humanity's tendency to ignore and deny things outside their experience does most of the work on its own. One's Masquerade is the personal effort a vampire makes to maintain a facade of humanity. The Julii claim credit for inventing the concept, and whether or not they were really the first vampires to pretend to be human, they certainly played a large role in popularizing the practice. The closest you'll really see to The Masquerade as a conspiracy rather than an individual practice in 2e is the re-envisioned Invictus, who style themselves the &quot;Conspiracy of Silence&quot; and work to cover up vampiric influence (and in particular, Invictus influence) in human power structures. This may all seem rather tangential to the subect at hand, but it serves an important role in properly framing the question of &quot;Does Masque = Masquerade?&quot; Heck, during open development Masque and Dirge were called Masquerade and Requiem respectively. I still think those would have been better names for the Traits, but ultimately they were changed to avoid confusion, since those words do refer to broader concepts than the Traits alone (and, you know, the two vampire gamelines). But the Traits are tied to those broader concepts, definitely.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>S. Brechen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/52522-regaining-willpower?p=901432#post901432\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The way I see it, The mask isn't just the face a vampire shows humans, it's the part of themselves they consciously or unconsciously show everyone, vampire or human. The Dirge would be what they keep for themselves or what they only allow themselves to be around people they trust. Regaining willpower from your mask is just a matter of how mcuh you're willing to risk to keep people from seeing beyond what you want them to see. Like, if a vampire has mask : mastermind, he'll get his kicks from people seeing him as a clever dude who's really difficult to outsmart. If one of his plans start to completely fall appart, he might regain all his willpower if he risks his unlife doing damage control and tying up loose ends so that nobody ever knows he messed up.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed. The Masque isn't just the face you wear among humans, it's the face you wear no matter who you are interacting with. I think the same is true with The Masquerade - it's not merely an effort one makes to keep one's vampiric nature a secret, it's the effort one makes to appear human. And if you think about how vampires behave among themselves, they're still trying to keep up that veneer of humanity. Sure, they don't waste effort trying to hide the fact that they're undead and that they drink blood. But they have laws forbidding the use of Disciplines against each other, or attacking each other in fits of Frenzy. They make just as much effort to control their Beasts among other Kindred as they do among Kine, if not more. They construct and engage in elaborate social structures that are as removed as you can get from their true, Bestial natures. They want to convince each other (and ultimately, themselves) that they are basically just humans suffering from an unfortunate condition that makes them highly averse to sunlight and require regular blood transfusions. So, the Masquerade is just as much a practice you engage in among other vampires as it is one you use to keep your secret safe from the muggles. Accordingly, the Masque is the persona you present to the world to distract it from who you really are, your Dirge.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>S. Brechen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/52522-regaining-willpower?p=901432#post901432\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">People might disagree on the exact meaning, but I'm pretty sure it's not about the masquerade. One of my player's character has the Mask : Harmless and the Dirge : Vindictive. She's a former vampire hunter turned vampire herself. She tries to appear pretty harmless to everyone she meets but has a pretty mean streak when she feels people have crossed her, including (in my game, mostly) vampires. She's mostly gained willpower by being vindictive so far, but if she, for example, let herself get beat up by someone without really trying to fight back, she'd regain willpower because she wouldn't look like a threat.</div> </div> </div> </div>That sounds like a fun character, and a great example of how Masque and Dirge can interact. Don't get me wrong here, I think we're ultimately agreeing on what Masque and Dirge represent and how they are meant to be used. We're just disagreeing on what the concept of Masquerade means to vampires, and I would argue that one's Masque plays a big role in her Masquerade.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>S. Brechen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/52522-regaining-willpower?p=901432#post901432\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is an example, but the mask and dirge don't have to be opposite or really different. Again, though, I wouldn't be too attached to that. These are two ways to see your character, but any believable character won't be described by just two words.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree for the most part, although I think it's important that they not be exactly the same. This is where Masque and Dirge differ from Requem's Nature and Demeanor. Your Masque is the side you want people to see, as well as the person you want to believe yourself to be. Dirge is who you let yourself be when you think no one is watching, it's the unlife you lead that you wouldn't want people to find out about, the reason you participate in The Masquerade in the first place. If they were exactly the same (apart from giving you effectively half as many ways to regain Willpower), you would have no reason to take part in the Masquerade. You could simply present yourself as you truly are to everyone around you, vampire and mortal alike.<br /> <br /> On a side note, this gives me ideas for Dark Eras games set before the Camarilla.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>S. Brechen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/52522-regaining-willpower?p=901432#post901432\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is beside the point, but I think it's also pretty normal for character to change their mask or dirge occasionnally if it's justified. One of my players who had the dirge &amp;quot;humanist&amp;quot; (she would always try to favor humans, seeing vampires as monsters that needed to be killed if they didn't try really hard to not feed on humans) asked to change it after she found out about the Strix, how they were potentially way worse than the vampires and that vampires were maybe one of the few things that had a shot at fighting them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Totally. I don't know if the rules specifically call out that option, but I firmly believe it should be allowed whenever appropriate to the story.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-27T17:43:44-07:00","id":901573,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/52522-regaining-willpower?p=901516#post901516\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Eeeyyyyhhhh, that's kind of an outdated concept of the Masquerade at this point. That's certainly what it means in VtM, and 1e kind of held onto it, but 2e has really doubled down on the idea that the supernatural doesn't need a massive concerted effort to keep itself secret. Humanity's tendency to ignore and deny things outside their experience does most of the work on its own. One's Masquerade is the personal effort a vampire makes to maintain a facade of humanity. The Julii claim credit for inventing the concept, and whether or not they were really the first vampires to pretend to be human, they certainly played a large role in popularizing the practice. The closest you'll really see to The Masquerade as a conspiracy rather than an individual practice in 2e is the re-envisioned Invictus, who style themselves the &quot;Conspiracy of Silence&quot; and work to cover up vampiric influence (and in particular, Invictus influence) in human power structures. This may all seem rather tangential to the subect at hand, but it serves an important role in properly framing the question of &quot;Does Masque = Masquerade?&quot; Heck, during open development Masque and Dirge were called Masquerade and Requiem respectively. I still think those would have been better names for the Traits, but ultimately they were changed to avoid confusion, since those words do refer to broader concepts than the Traits alone (and, you know, the two vampire gamelines). But the Traits are tied to those broader concepts, definitely.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's interesting, didn't know about the masquerade/requiem being the prototype mask and dirge, but it makes a lot of sense. And yeah, you're right that the masquerade isn't some grand conspiracy in the book, especially since the vampires not having centralized government beyond cities (unless you want them to in your game of course) doesn't allow for such a system to exist. That said, it's still among the traditions along with embracing and diablerie. Obviously, traditions is all they are. Vampires embrace all the time and diablerize way more often than reasonnable (which would be never but whatevs). It's interesting that they went even further towards the small scale aspect o the masquerade in the 2nd Edition.<br /> <br /> That said, I had this feeling reading some of the 1st edition material that, as you said, there is not much need for an active conspiracy, like mortals in general actually don't really want to know and they usually will forget or rationnalize most of what they see unless you actually get in their face. In that regard, breaking the masquerade in a way that would actually threaten a city (or more) would probably require some hard work to pull off between mortals' basic rationnality, the other kindred breaking your knees to teach you not to mess around and the hunters that are likely to get you once you've made your presence felt but before a meaningful number of people actually discover anything.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/52522-regaining-willpower?p=901516#post901516\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I agree for the most part, although I think it's important that they not be exactly the same. This is where Masque and Dirge differ from Requem's Nature and Demeanor. Your Masque is the side you want people to see, as well as the person you want to believe yourself to be. Dirge is who you let yourself be when you think no one is watching, it's the unlife you lead that you wouldn't want people to find out about, the reason you participate in The Masquerade in the first place. If they were exactly the same (apart from giving you effectively half as many ways to regain Willpower), you would have no reason to take part in the Masquerade. You could simply present yourself as you truly are to everyone around you, vampire and mortal alike.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's definitely more fun if they're not the same for most characters. Having them being the same, though (aside from it being mechanically disadvantageous) could be interesting in a few cases, though. It could be the end of a path for a character that ends up finding a sort of personnal balance, good or bad. An ancient vampire could display exactly what they are, confident that those who shouldn't know the truth won't be able to grasp or handle it anyway so why bother to lie to them ? Just an idea like that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7104-s-brechen","name":"S. Brechen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"171"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}